```
Reason:
The variable `i` was declared outside of the loop, which caused it to retain its value across multiple iterations. This improper handling meant that the checks on `i` were ineffective, leading to incorrect behavior in determining the length of the stream, as `i` was not being reset correctly for each loop.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
int i = 0;
```
```c
