```
```c
for( int i = 0; i < PS_TK_COUNT; i++ )
```
Reason:
By declaring `i` within the scope of the loop (using `int i = 0;`), it ensures that `i` is reset to 0 for each new iteration of the loop. This change allows the checks on `i` to function correctly, ensuring that the function behaves as intended when determining the length of the stream.


